cff-version: 1.2.0
title: adapter-extraction-testbed
message: >-
  A reproducible testbed for measuring model extraction and abstention
  transfer against a task-specific LoRA adapter, with an experimental
  defense mechanism.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Jason
    family-names: Wong
repository-code: "https://github.com/JASONW26327/adapter-extraction-testbed"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Measures how many API-style queries are needed to clone the behaviour of a
  fine-tuned adapter, and whether the adapter's refusal behaviour transfers to
  the stolen copy. Uses a synthetic corpus generated from a documented rule so
  the model's decision function is known exactly and extraction can be measured
  rather than asserted. Compares DistilGPT-2 and Gemma 3 4B backbones, includes
  a 100-prompt categorized adversarial suite, and experiments with output
  perturbation as a query-rate-limited defense against extraction.
keywords:
  - model extraction
  - model stealing
  - LoRA
  - AI security
  - abstention
  - prompt injection
  - instruction hierarchy
  - Gemma 3
